question:
AITA Gave my daughter's friend cupcakes? Last week my daughter had a friend over. Her parents are very anti-sugar, and have told me this many times in the past. Today after school my daughter brought her friend over. As an after-school snack I like to sometimes make cupcakes. My daughter took one and enjoyed it very much. I offered some to her friend, and she accepted it. She clearly doesn't ever have sugar, liked them a lot, and ended up eating 6 in one sitting. After we took her home, I got an angry text from her parents saying "How dare you let her have sugar" and she isn't allowed at my house in the near future. My daughter got very upset when she heard the news. AITA?

&#x200B;

edit because this looks like it will be a thing: I left the plate of cupcakes on a counter in the kitchen. I did not know how many she ate until after.

&#x200B;

edit 2: They're 13 if that helps
